er annabelle what you make of of  with this new uh plan from the  government they're talking about their  slim down you know trying to reduce the  size of uh government  trying to obviously move the focus from  the crises that they've been jumping  between to actually  the job that they're there to do which  is to govern the country uh do you like  the plan  um well anything that that slims down  the size of the government uh gets my  support for sure i mean in terms of this  story obviously we've got to bear in  mind that it is in the scottish  national um what's interesting is how  incense the scottish people still are  about partygate one poll and the article  found that more than three quarters of  scots think that boris johnson should  resign while just 15  think he should stay  obviously he's got a serious problem  with the leader of the scottish  conservatives and he's going to have to  go to scotland and embark on a strategy  of appeasement there but i think when it  comes to taking on the smp uh boris  johnson has got to go on the offensive  he's got to remind the scottish people  about uh the snp's performance on the  economy on covid on civil liberties on  education all those uh areas where in my  view at least the snp has  been left wanting um so you know  obviously it's going to be a very  challenging week arguably the prime  minister would be on more comfortable  territory believe it or not negotiating  and um engaging in diplomacy with uh the  situation in ukraine more than going to  scotland and trying to face uh the  scottish people and put forward his  leveling up agenda to them but it it's  going to be a challenging week for him  one way or the other but i do think it's  it's very important that he goes uh to  scotland and starts to try and rally  support there  i want to quickly try and squeeze in one  more uh story here from the front the  front page of the financial times  shoppers undeterred as big brands raise  prices to protect profits from 